1
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:35,009
[Forging Justice]

2
00:01:35,190 --> 00:01:37,750
[Episode 29]

3
00:01:48,789 --> 00:01:50,920
Why didn't you go home?

4
00:01:52,150 --> 00:01:52,610
Go home?

5
00:01:53,350 --> 00:01:55,009
What home? I don't have a home.

6
00:01:58,640 --> 00:01:59,970
Have you been drinking?

7
00:02:01,130 --> 00:02:02,350
I went out to eat with some friends

8
00:02:02,350 --> 00:02:03,080
and had a sip.

9
00:02:04,310 --> 00:02:05,640
What have you been up to?

10
00:02:06,220 --> 00:02:07,090
I reorganized

11
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:08,500
some files.

12
00:02:08,570 --> 00:02:09,810
And went over some

13
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:10,520
old cases

14
00:02:10,910 --> 00:02:11,970
to learn from them.

15
00:02:12,710 --> 00:02:14,570
You just can't sit still, can you?

16
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:35,690
My wife went to Beijing,

17
00:02:40,150 --> 00:02:41,410
for a foreign company.

18
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:43,800
She might not come back.

19
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:44,840
Isn't that funny?

20
00:02:46,150 --> 00:02:47,430
I was the one
who always wanted to go to Beijing.

21
00:02:47,430 --> 00:02:48,760
And in the end, she went.

22
00:02:57,490 --> 00:02:58,950
What about your daughter?

23
00:02:59,110 --> 00:03:00,570
She's at home, doing fine.

24
00:03:02,190 --> 00:03:03,250
At a time like this,

25
00:03:03,710 --> 00:03:05,570
a daughter needs her dad the most.

26
00:03:06,910 --> 00:03:07,240
Here.

27
00:03:08,710 --> 00:03:10,400
Have some water, take a moment,

28
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:12,200
then go home and be with your kid.

29
00:03:25,590 --> 00:03:26,790
Can we talk a bit more?

30
00:03:31,910 --> 00:03:32,520
I don't mean anything else.

31
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:33,450
I'm feeling really down.

32
00:03:33,450 --> 00:03:35,050
Just need someone to talk to.

33
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:39,630
In Binjiang, you're the only one

34
00:03:39,630 --> 00:03:40,680
I can open up to.

35
00:03:48,240 --> 00:03:50,170
Yizhong and Lu are in Binjiang too.

36
00:03:51,310 --> 00:03:51,910
Can't you open up

37
00:03:51,910 --> 00:03:52,800
to them?

38
00:03:54,470 --> 00:03:55,380
You three

39
00:03:55,630 --> 00:03:57,090
were close back in school.

40
00:04:04,910 --> 00:04:06,040
Yu, you've actually

41
00:04:06,870 --> 00:04:08,360
had a lot in life.

42
00:04:10,720 --> 00:04:11,560
But you never look at

43
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:13,160
what's right in front of you.

44
00:04:14,630 --> 00:04:15,910
You keep moving forward

45
00:04:15,910 --> 00:04:17,709
and losing things along the way.

46
00:04:18,390 --> 00:04:19,190
Is it worth it?

47
00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:28,560
Go home.

48
00:04:38,870 --> 00:04:40,820
Turn off the light for me, will you?

49
00:05:03,430 --> 00:05:04,630
It's really hard to find any new

50
00:05:04,630 --> 00:05:06,090
evidence in this case now.

51
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:08,190
From what you see so far,

52
00:05:08,190 --> 00:05:08,750
first,

53
00:05:09,510 --> 00:05:11,070
no blood on the murder weapon.

54
00:05:11,070 --> 00:05:11,530
Second,

55
00:05:11,870 --> 00:05:14,000
the wound isn't unique to that weapon.

56
00:05:14,490 --> 00:05:15,400
Even the blood

57
00:05:15,430 --> 00:05:16,800
on Hu Xudong's shirt

58
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,330
might not be Yin Ping's.

59
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:19,920
You don't even trust

60
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:20,950
the forensic report?

61
00:05:20,950 --> 00:05:22,160
That's not a definitive result.

62
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:23,760
It's just an expert opinion.

63
00:05:24,120 --> 00:05:25,680
And with the current

64
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:26,950
blood typing technology,

65
00:05:26,950 --> 00:05:28,120
even in the UK,

66
00:05:28,310 --> 00:05:28,950
the error rate

67
00:05:28,950 --> 00:05:29,750
would be 20%.

68
00:05:30,150 --> 00:05:31,040
So you're convinced

69
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:31,920
this case falls into

70
00:05:31,920 --> 00:05:32,750
that 20%?

71
00:05:33,070 --> 00:05:34,330
What makes you so sure?

72
00:05:34,830 --> 00:05:35,750
Are we in the UK?

73
00:05:36,510 --> 00:05:37,360
No, well,

74
00:05:37,380 --> 00:05:38,750
in Hu Xudong's confession,

75
00:05:38,750 --> 00:05:40,750
he mentioned that the three buttons

76
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:42,390
fell off
during the struggle with Yin Ping,

77
00:05:42,390 --> 00:05:43,750
and he picked them up after the murder.

78
00:05:43,750 --> 00:05:45,409
We went to the scene yesterday.

79
00:05:45,409 --> 00:05:46,480
We did an experiment after dark.

80
00:05:46,480 --> 00:05:48,159
It's pitch black there after dark,

81
00:05:48,159 --> 00:05:49,120
you can't see anything.

82
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:50,070
Let alone three buttons,

83
00:05:50,070 --> 00:05:50,830
even if you threw three pancakes,

84
00:05:50,830 --> 00:05:51,800
I wouldn't be able to find them.

85
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:53,260
Maybe he had a flashlight.

86
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,430
None of the records,

87
00:05:55,510 --> 00:05:57,260
including Hu Xudong's own confession,

88
00:05:57,260 --> 00:05:58,520
mention a flashlight.

89
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:02,610
Then let's wait.

90
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:06,610
Wait for
the supplementary investigation results.

91
00:06:07,390 --> 00:06:08,920
Anyway, based on the current evidence,

92
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:10,720
we don't have any solid evidence

93
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:11,310
to prove

94
00:06:11,310 --> 00:06:12,650
that Hu Xudong killed him.

95
00:06:12,650 --> 00:06:13,650
You know that too.

96
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:15,620
What are you trying to say?

97
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:16,380
I'm saying,

98
00:06:16,770 --> 00:06:18,000
is it possible that the procuratorate

99
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:19,860
might withdraw the prosecution?

100
00:06:26,430 --> 00:06:28,240
There's an Arabian folktale collection

101
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:29,210
called "One Thousand and One Nights",

102
00:06:29,210 --> 00:06:30,800
also known as "Arabian Nights".

103
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:32,659
Yizhong, you're too idealistic.

104
00:06:37,680 --> 00:06:38,610
What do you mean?

105
00:06:40,240 --> 00:06:41,310
What do you mean?

106
00:06:41,750 --> 00:06:43,000
Did you send Yang?

107
00:06:44,830 --> 00:06:45,390
Where?

108
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:48,480
To Jiangbei to investigate Jia Peng.

109
00:06:48,480 --> 00:06:49,000
Yes.

110
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:51,570
Zhang Hongshan, get up.

111
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:54,159
Are you blind?

112
00:06:54,450 --> 00:06:56,180
Didn't you see my clothes here?

113
00:06:56,260 --> 00:06:57,000
I'm going to my daughter's

114
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:57,830
parent-teacher meeting later.

115
00:06:57,830 --> 00:06:58,430
Geez.

116
00:06:58,950 --> 00:06:59,750
Jiang Bin.

117
00:06:59,950 --> 00:07:01,240
Your mentor has gone crazy.

118
00:07:01,240 --> 00:07:02,900
Don't let him lead you astray.

119
00:07:04,160 --> 00:07:05,310
Show some respect.

120
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:06,520
Call me Chief.

121
00:07:08,420 --> 00:07:09,570
Chief Jiang,

122
00:07:10,160 --> 00:07:11,390
if you side with outsiders,

123
00:07:11,390 --> 00:07:13,000
your authority will be affected.

124
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,920
If the higher-ups find out
you've been digging on your own,

125
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:17,050
you'll have to
face the consequences.

126
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:22,940
Did I say
I was reopening the investigation?

127
00:07:23,920 --> 00:07:25,870
Just looking into Jia Peng's information

128
00:07:25,870 --> 00:07:28,040
is perfectly legal and aboveboard.

129
00:07:28,630 --> 00:07:29,920
What's wrong with that?

130
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:31,250
What have you found out?

131
00:07:31,510 --> 00:07:32,820
Jia Peng should have
been executed long ago.

132
00:07:32,820 --> 00:07:34,550
Why hasn't it been carried out?

133
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:37,920
Well, Jia Peng

134
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:40,920
appealed as soon as
he was sentenced to death.

135
00:07:40,920 --> 00:07:41,920
After the review,

136
00:07:42,290 --> 00:07:42,970
he said

137
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,830
he had major case details to confess.

138
00:07:44,830 --> 00:07:45,430
He said

139
00:07:45,680 --> 00:07:47,680
he not only killed those three girls,

140
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:49,240
but also robbed a taxi.

141
00:07:50,240 --> 00:07:52,800
So that meant
a retrial and more investigation.

142
00:07:52,800 --> 00:07:53,770
And now I hear

143
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:55,300
he's going to report his cellmates'

144
00:07:55,300 --> 00:07:56,100
other crimes.

145
00:07:56,870 --> 00:07:58,240
With all this back and forth,

146
00:07:58,240 --> 00:08:00,040
it's been dragged out until now.

147
00:08:00,510 --> 00:08:01,270
Right now

148
00:08:02,050 --> 00:08:03,000
he's just living one more day

149
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:03,830
at a time.

150
00:08:05,430 --> 00:08:07,290
Then what about Yan Jicai's case?

151
00:08:09,430 --> 00:08:10,960
You finally figured it out?

152
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:12,300
If he really did it,

153
00:08:12,430 --> 00:08:14,890
he'll confess
sooner or later to stay alive.

154
00:08:17,430 --> 00:08:18,950
And when that happens,

155
00:08:20,960 --> 00:08:22,360
we'll be on the back foot.

156
00:08:28,430 --> 00:08:29,360
Hey, Big Bottle.

157
00:08:30,120 --> 00:08:31,250
What's on your mind?

158
00:08:32,549 --> 00:08:33,390
Still thinking about

159
00:08:33,390 --> 00:08:34,720
that Prosecutor Zhang?

160
00:08:36,750 --> 00:08:37,750
Big Bottle,

161
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:39,720
let's be realistic.

162
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:42,080
She's married now, living her own life.

163
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:44,440
Goes home after work,
gets into bed with her husband.

164
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:46,240
You think she's got time for you?

165
00:08:47,570 --> 00:08:49,420
Even if they let you out first,

166
00:08:50,240 --> 00:08:51,390
do you think your wife would wait?

167
00:08:51,390 --> 00:08:51,720
Yeah.

168
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:53,600
She probably remarried long ago.

169
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:54,860
She couldn't hold out.

170
00:08:54,960 --> 00:08:55,360
Right?

171
00:08:57,870 --> 00:08:58,800
What's with you?

172
00:08:59,670 --> 00:09:01,200
Why are you hitting people?

173
00:09:07,750 --> 00:09:08,550
What are you doing?

174
00:09:08,550 --> 00:09:09,010
Stop it!

175
00:09:09,630 --> 00:09:10,490
Stop fighting!

176
00:09:10,720 --> 00:09:11,380
Squat down!

177
00:09:11,870 --> 00:09:12,530
Squat down!

178
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:14,910
Everyone, step back!

179
00:09:14,910 --> 00:09:16,120
Squat down! Hands on your head!

180
00:09:16,120 --> 00:09:16,600
Stop fighting!

181
00:09:16,600 --> 00:09:17,550
Yan Jicai, let go!

182
00:09:17,550 --> 00:09:18,210
Squat down!

183
00:09:18,790 --> 00:09:19,630
Everyone, squat down!

184
00:09:19,630 --> 00:09:20,290
Squat down!

185
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:25,720
Yan Jicai.

186
00:09:26,870 --> 00:09:28,800
You've only behaved for a few days.

187
00:09:28,910 --> 00:09:30,440
Why are you acting up again?

188
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:32,270
What's wrong with you?

189
00:09:32,270 --> 00:09:33,930
Do you want a longer sentence?

190
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:37,630
I want to see Prosecutor Guo.

191
00:09:37,630 --> 00:09:38,550
You want to see Prosecutor Guo

192
00:09:38,550 --> 00:09:39,480
for everything.

193
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:40,480
What if Prosecutor Guo

194
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:41,480
is no longer here?

195
00:09:41,870 --> 00:09:43,470
Are you going to stop living?

196
00:09:44,820 --> 00:09:45,710
Say that again.

197
00:09:46,910 --> 00:09:47,580
Guard Sun.

198
00:09:48,870 --> 00:09:49,600
I haven't seen Prosecutor Guo

199
00:09:49,600 --> 00:09:50,670
for a long time.

200
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:52,920
Guard Sun, be honest with me.

201
00:09:53,340 --> 00:09:54,470
Has he given up on me?

202
00:09:54,670 --> 00:09:55,750
He's fine.

203
00:09:56,480 --> 00:09:58,080
He just went on an urgent business trip.

204
00:09:58,080 --> 00:09:58,600
Before he left,

205
00:09:58,600 --> 00:09:59,840
he specifically told me

206
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:01,030
to have you behave

207
00:10:01,270 --> 00:10:02,360
and not cause any trouble.

208
00:10:02,360 --> 00:10:04,690
That's the only way
you won't let him down.

209
00:10:05,320 --> 00:10:06,780
That last part was from me.

210
00:10:06,930 --> 00:10:08,260
Think it over yourself.

211
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:13,550
Hello?

212
00:10:14,010 --> 00:10:14,790
This is the Prosecutor's Office

213
00:10:14,790 --> 00:10:15,850
at Bieshan Prison.

214
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:17,870
Who is looking for Prosecutor Guo?

215
00:10:17,870 --> 00:10:18,320
I am.

216
00:10:18,550 --> 00:10:19,480
I'm Zhang Lihui.

217
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:21,800
Please wait a moment.

218
00:10:22,670 --> 00:10:23,150
Ms. Liu,

219
00:10:23,640 --> 00:10:24,790
someone named Zhang Lihui

220
00:10:24,790 --> 00:10:26,050
is calling for Mr. Guo.

221
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:28,450
Give it to me.

222
00:10:32,080 --> 00:10:32,880
Lihui, right?

223
00:10:32,910 --> 00:10:33,640
Yes, it's me.

224
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:34,690
It's Liu Wei.

225
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:35,870
Ms. Liu,

226
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:37,300
where is my mentor?

227
00:10:38,310 --> 00:10:39,240
He's on a business trip.

228
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:39,840
A long one.

229
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:42,570
Somewhere down south, I think.

230
00:10:42,870 --> 00:10:43,960
Not sure if it's Guangzhou

231
00:10:43,960 --> 00:10:44,690
or Shenzhen.

232
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:46,060
He didn't specify.

233
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:48,400
He won't be back for two or three months.

234
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:50,120
Why didn't he

235
00:10:50,150 --> 00:10:51,030
tell me?

236
00:10:51,670 --> 00:10:52,120
Ms. Liu,

237
00:10:52,120 --> 00:10:53,720
do you have his number there?

238
00:10:54,550 --> 00:10:55,410
I really don't.

239
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:56,660
Okay, I see.

240
00:10:56,910 --> 00:10:57,970
Thank you, Ms. Liu.

241
00:11:06,670 --> 00:11:07,130
Ms. Liu,

242
00:11:07,960 --> 00:11:09,890
what day is Mr. Guo having surgery?

243
00:11:12,150 --> 00:11:12,670
Today.

244
00:11:16,100 --> 00:11:18,460
[Inpatient Department]

245
00:11:19,560 --> 00:11:20,530
Hold on.

246
00:11:23,080 --> 00:11:23,600
Guo,

247
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:25,410
don't be afraid.

248
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:26,450
Don't worry.

249
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:28,720
We'll all be waiting right outside.

250
00:11:28,790 --> 00:11:29,590
It'll go well.

251
00:11:29,870 --> 00:11:30,330
It will.

252
00:11:32,320 --> 00:11:33,180
I'm not afraid.

253
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:37,020
I'm just worried Lihui
will come looking for me.

254
00:11:38,870 --> 00:11:39,800
What will you do?

255
00:11:40,120 --> 00:11:41,700
Y-You repeat it.

256
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:42,940
I'll hold it in.

257
00:11:43,480 --> 00:11:44,480
I won't say a word.

258
00:11:46,720 --> 00:11:47,440
And you?

259
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:49,260
I'll remind the prison again.

260
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:51,320
Make sure they don't tell Yan Jicai.

261
00:11:51,540 --> 00:11:51,880
Wait,

262
00:11:51,910 --> 00:11:53,570
did you actually remind them?

263
00:11:53,630 --> 00:11:55,320
Don't you trust me?

264
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:58,200
I'm just worried.

265
00:11:58,720 --> 00:11:59,920
Just shut up. Shut up.

266
00:12:00,270 --> 00:12:01,330
At a time like this,

267
00:12:01,390 --> 00:12:03,590
you're still thinking about an inmate.

268
00:12:03,840 --> 00:12:06,100
I'm afraid he might do something stupid.

269
00:12:06,960 --> 00:12:08,480
He takes things too hard.

270
00:12:09,840 --> 00:12:11,440
If he finds out I have cancer,

271
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:11,880
he'll—

272
00:12:12,200 --> 00:12:14,400
Please stop talking. It's time to go in.

273
00:12:14,870 --> 00:12:15,380
Guo.

274
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:15,840
Please wait here.

275
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:16,150
Guo.

276
00:12:16,150 --> 00:12:16,550
It's fine.

277
00:12:16,550 --> 00:12:17,550
Please wait here.

278
00:12:29,270 --> 00:12:30,960
Mentor, where did you
go on your business trip?

279
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:31,890
I couldn't reach you.

280
00:12:31,890 --> 00:12:33,340
Worried. Please reply.

281
00:12:34,670 --> 00:12:35,400
Captain Lyu.

282
00:12:37,150 --> 00:12:37,880
You're here.

283
00:12:38,630 --> 00:12:39,290
Have a seat.

284
00:12:39,390 --> 00:12:39,990
Thank you.

285
00:12:42,120 --> 00:12:43,250
Here, have some tea.

286
00:12:43,550 --> 00:12:44,200
Thank you.

287
00:12:46,550 --> 00:12:48,320
How is Siyi recovering?

288
00:12:50,390 --> 00:12:52,050
Good. She's recovering well.

289
00:12:53,320 --> 00:12:55,450
The doctor said it's very optimistic.

290
00:12:55,550 --> 00:12:56,150
Thank you.

291
00:12:57,270 --> 00:12:59,240
Thank you for always caring about her.

292
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:00,640
It's the least I could do.

293
00:13:01,810 --> 00:13:02,720
You don't want to do gymnastics.

294
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:03,650
I totally get it.

295
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:06,580
My dream was to be a lawyer.

296
00:13:07,270 --> 00:13:09,270
I even went to law school for it.

297
00:13:09,360 --> 00:13:10,160
And then what?

298
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:12,200
As soon as I graduated,

299
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:14,360
my dad refused to let me be a lawyer.

300
00:13:15,550 --> 00:13:16,030
Why?

301
00:13:16,550 --> 00:13:18,810
He didn't want me to repeat his mistakes.

302
00:13:19,600 --> 00:13:20,400
He meant well,

303
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:23,720
but it's also pretty sad.

304
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:25,840
By the way,

305
00:13:26,440 --> 00:13:27,790
you didn't become a lawyer,

306
00:13:27,790 --> 00:13:28,720
so what do you do?

307
00:13:30,240 --> 00:13:31,240
I'm a journalist.

308
00:13:32,430 --> 00:13:32,910
So

309
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:36,000
you didn't come here to skip stones?

310
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:36,630
No.

311
00:13:38,720 --> 00:13:40,580
Your mom even threw ketchup at me.

312
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:42,630
That was you?

313
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:43,820
Yeah, it was me.

314
00:13:46,150 --> 00:13:46,810
Just leave.

315
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:50,880
I don't want to lie to you,

316
00:13:51,290 --> 00:13:52,080
but I really wasn't

317
00:13:52,080 --> 00:13:52,720
scheming—

318
00:13:52,740 --> 00:13:53,460
Go away!

319
00:13:57,910 --> 00:13:59,970
There's one thing I'd like to ask you.

320
00:14:00,270 --> 00:14:00,790
You see,

321
00:14:01,200 --> 00:14:02,330
my daughter Lyu Siyi

322
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:03,670
chose to kill herself

323
00:14:03,720 --> 00:14:05,050
to prove her innocence.

324
00:14:07,150 --> 00:14:08,360
Does that mean

325
00:14:09,150 --> 00:14:10,350
Wang Danni was lying?

326
00:14:12,430 --> 00:14:14,910
To be honest,
and don't take this the wrong way,

327
00:14:14,910 --> 00:14:16,840
without witnesses,
it's a Rashomon situation.

328
00:14:16,840 --> 00:14:18,100
Anything is possible.

329
00:14:19,910 --> 00:14:21,840
That's exactly what I want to hear.

330
00:14:22,630 --> 00:14:23,480
By that logic,

331
00:14:23,750 --> 00:14:25,150
even if Yan Jicai killed himself

332
00:14:25,150 --> 00:14:25,790
in prison,

333
00:14:26,320 --> 00:14:27,390
that wouldn't prove

334
00:14:27,390 --> 00:14:28,650
his innocence either,

335
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:29,120
right?

336
00:14:30,270 --> 00:14:31,000
Captain Lyu,

337
00:14:31,480 --> 00:14:32,540
that's different.

338
00:14:32,760 --> 00:14:33,550
How is it different?

339
00:14:33,550 --> 00:14:34,750
Just hearing him cry foul,

340
00:14:34,750 --> 00:14:36,480
we wouldn't easily believe it.

341
00:14:37,270 --> 00:14:38,510
A lot of evidence shows

342
00:14:38,510 --> 00:14:40,310
that Yan Jicai is not the killer.

343
00:14:40,910 --> 00:14:42,370
Let me put it the other way,

344
00:14:42,790 --> 00:14:43,990
the current evidence

345
00:14:44,150 --> 00:14:45,120
cannot prove

346
00:14:45,150 --> 00:14:46,750
that Yan Jicai is the killer.

347
00:14:48,790 --> 00:14:50,120
Then let me ask you this,

348
00:14:50,870 --> 00:14:51,320
if

349
00:14:52,200 --> 00:14:54,000
either Wang Danni

350
00:14:54,870 --> 00:14:55,770
or my daughter

351
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:57,260
Lyu Siyi must be lying,

352
00:14:57,910 --> 00:14:59,640
who do you think is more likely?

353
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:01,330
I think your assumption

354
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:02,360
is wrong.

355
00:15:02,870 --> 00:15:03,730
How is it wrong?

356
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:05,480
One of them must be lying?

357
00:15:05,870 --> 00:15:07,240
Why can't both of them

358
00:15:07,270 --> 00:15:08,470
be telling the truth?

359
00:15:09,270 --> 00:15:10,320
How is that possible?

360
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:11,450
Maybe they mis-saw,

361
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:12,600
misremembered,

362
00:15:12,600 --> 00:15:13,400
or misjudged.

363
00:15:13,750 --> 00:15:15,810
Maybe it was all a misunderstanding.

364
00:15:16,750 --> 00:15:17,910
Then that misunderstanding would have

365
00:15:17,910 --> 00:15:18,910
cost far too much.

366
00:15:19,790 --> 00:15:21,270
As for Yan Jicai's case,

367
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:25,200
I've been reflecting on myself lately.

368
00:15:25,570 --> 00:15:26,690
Have I been

369
00:15:26,720 --> 00:15:27,720
too stubborn

370
00:15:27,750 --> 00:15:28,880
and too subjective?

371
00:15:30,320 --> 00:15:31,520
But there is one thing

372
00:15:32,110 --> 00:15:33,670
I have never wavered on.

373
00:15:35,150 --> 00:15:35,750
We

374
00:15:36,240 --> 00:15:37,440
should do our best

375
00:15:37,720 --> 00:15:38,720
to give this case,

376
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:40,480
give Yan Jicai,

377
00:15:40,510 --> 00:15:42,170
and give the law

378
00:15:42,240 --> 00:15:43,270
a fair chance,

379
00:15:44,080 --> 00:15:44,870
to fight for a

380
00:15:45,150 --> 00:15:46,750
retrial that can convince

381
00:15:47,030 --> 00:15:48,160
our own conscience.

382
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,360
As for the result,

383
00:15:52,840 --> 00:15:54,500
that matters less, actually.

384
00:16:00,750 --> 00:16:01,810
Prosecutor Zhang,

385
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:03,750
I've done my best

386
00:16:04,390 --> 00:16:05,360
on this case.

387
00:16:06,790 --> 00:16:08,600
What I can do now is very limited.

388
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:11,700
But at the same time, I want to say,

389
00:16:11,720 --> 00:16:13,380
it's been an honor to know you.

390
00:16:13,670 --> 00:16:14,390
I've learned

391
00:16:14,390 --> 00:16:15,550
a lot from you.

392
00:16:17,200 --> 00:16:17,800
Thank you.

393
00:16:19,510 --> 00:16:20,150
Captain Lyu.

394
00:16:20,150 --> 00:16:21,810
I've already paid for the tea.

395
00:16:22,270 --> 00:16:22,800
Goodbye.

396
00:16:24,440 --> 00:16:24,970
Goodbye.

397
00:16:25,910 --> 00:16:26,440
Goodbye.

398
00:16:33,390 --> 00:16:34,920
This is our search warrant.

399
00:16:51,890 --> 00:16:52,820
Let me see that.

400
00:16:53,080 --> 00:16:55,410
What are you doing with this crappy glove?

401
00:16:56,670 --> 00:16:58,330
I'll call the police station.

402
00:17:04,770 --> 00:17:06,230
Captain Wang, we found it.

403
00:17:10,750 --> 00:17:11,440
Put this on.

404
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:15,099
Which hand?

405
00:17:15,530 --> 00:17:16,260
Left hand.

406
00:17:23,400 --> 00:17:24,260
Take a picture.

407
00:17:29,590 --> 00:17:30,920
These two aren't a pair.

408
00:17:31,230 --> 00:17:32,410
Just put them on.

409
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:39,500
Take a picture.

410
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:43,070
If you ask me,

411
00:17:43,680 --> 00:17:45,010
just this pair of gloves

412
00:17:45,270 --> 00:17:46,870
is enough to press charges.

413
00:17:48,440 --> 00:17:48,790
Lin.

414
00:17:49,800 --> 00:17:50,830
Are you still insisting

415
00:17:50,830 --> 00:17:53,290
on another supplementary investigation?

416
00:18:26,640 --> 00:18:27,160
Lu.

417
00:18:29,110 --> 00:18:29,550
Lu!

418
00:18:30,530 --> 00:18:30,970
What?

419
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:31,600
Come here.

420
00:18:32,680 --> 00:18:33,240
Geez.

421
00:18:34,550 --> 00:18:36,200
What do you want?

422
00:18:37,510 --> 00:18:39,160
Put that down.

423
00:18:39,350 --> 00:18:39,750
Wait—

424
00:18:39,970 --> 00:18:41,750
Put that down, will you?

425
00:18:47,590 --> 00:18:48,720
Ow, ow, ow.

426
00:18:48,740 --> 00:18:49,060
Ow.

427
00:18:49,350 --> 00:18:51,480
Why are you poking me?

428
00:18:52,590 --> 00:18:53,240
See it now?

429
00:18:53,720 --> 00:18:55,450
I see it. You've lost your mind.

430
00:18:55,830 --> 00:18:56,750
What do you mean?

431
00:18:56,750 --> 00:18:57,500
See it or not?

432
00:19:01,110 --> 00:19:01,710
Left hand.

433
00:19:02,070 --> 00:19:03,670
I poked you with my left hand.

434
00:19:05,550 --> 00:19:06,540
Look, all your "wounds"

435
00:19:06,540 --> 00:19:08,680
are concentrated
on the right side of your abdomen,

436
00:19:08,680 --> 00:19:09,080
right?

437
00:19:10,780 --> 00:19:12,180
Yin Ping's were the same.

438
00:19:21,520 --> 00:19:22,050
Alright.

439
00:19:26,760 --> 00:19:28,650
[Registration Office]

440
00:19:28,320 --> 00:19:29,720
Hello, I'm his son.

441
00:19:30,480 --> 00:19:31,880
This is Prosecutor Chen—

442
00:19:31,940 --> 00:19:32,430
no,

443
00:19:33,240 --> 00:19:33,970
Lawyer Chen.

444
00:19:36,750 --> 00:19:37,160
Dad.

445
00:19:37,640 --> 00:19:38,750
Prosecutor Chen has been

446
00:19:38,750 --> 00:19:40,200
helping our family these past few years.

447
00:19:40,200 --> 00:19:43,130
He also helped me a lot
with my college entrance exam.

448
00:19:51,510 --> 00:19:52,350
Qiao Wu

449
00:19:53,270 --> 00:19:54,270
and Lame Zheng...

450
00:19:55,750 --> 00:19:56,510
Executed.

451
00:19:57,160 --> 00:19:58,750
They were executed half a year ago.

452
00:19:58,750 --> 00:20:00,740
You and your mentor sent them away?

453
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:02,350
I'm no longer at the procuratorate.

454
00:20:02,350 --> 00:20:03,480
I'm a lawyer now.

455
00:20:04,750 --> 00:20:05,810
They're both dead?

456
00:20:14,240 --> 00:20:15,880
Should I thank you for that?

457
00:20:16,510 --> 00:20:18,070
If I were still out there,

458
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:19,940
there'd be a third one.

459
00:20:23,690 --> 00:20:24,440
You didn't come see me

460
00:20:24,440 --> 00:20:26,170
because you missed me, did you?

461
00:20:27,920 --> 00:20:29,920
I need your help. Take a look at this.

462
00:20:37,400 --> 00:20:38,060
Who's this?

463
00:20:38,130 --> 00:20:39,440
Don't worry about who it is.

464
00:20:39,440 --> 00:20:41,400
Just treat him as the victim.

465
00:20:42,040 --> 00:20:42,880
The real victim

466
00:20:42,880 --> 00:20:43,960
was a little thinner than him,

467
00:20:43,960 --> 00:20:44,640
and

468
00:20:44,920 --> 00:20:45,920
a little shorter.

469
00:20:46,030 --> 00:20:47,290
Can you tell anything?

470
00:20:52,920 --> 00:20:53,880
The killer

471
00:20:54,720 --> 00:20:55,880
is left-handed.

472
00:20:56,790 --> 00:20:57,680
Left-handed.

473
00:20:58,270 --> 00:20:59,530
An expert with a knife.

474
00:20:59,950 --> 00:21:01,950
In your words, a habitual offender.

475
00:21:02,780 --> 00:21:03,750
How can you tell?

476
00:21:04,070 --> 00:21:04,550
Well,

477
00:21:05,310 --> 00:21:07,510
a rookie would stab wildly when panicked.

478
00:21:07,510 --> 00:21:08,270
This guy

479
00:21:08,720 --> 00:21:10,650
avoided the bones with every stab.

480
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:16,720
Could he stab like this in the dark?

481
00:21:16,720 --> 00:21:17,960
I could.

482
00:21:29,440 --> 00:21:30,000
Well,

483
00:21:30,830 --> 00:21:32,560
welcome back next time.

484
00:21:33,270 --> 00:21:35,350
Let me talk to my son.

485
00:21:35,780 --> 00:21:36,300
Right.

486
00:21:36,320 --> 00:21:37,720
Come on, talk to your dad.

487
00:21:39,790 --> 00:21:41,030
Are your studies going well?

488
00:21:41,030 --> 00:21:41,920
P-Pretty good.

489
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:44,590
Mr. Chen.

490
00:21:45,160 --> 00:21:47,360
Was my dad really called the Knife King?

491
00:21:47,510 --> 00:21:49,640
I only know your dad's surname is Wang.

492
00:21:49,640 --> 00:21:51,000
I've always heard people say

493
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:52,460
he's a legend in Binjiang.

494
00:21:53,790 --> 00:21:55,160
That's no legend.

495
00:21:55,680 --> 00:21:57,940
Your dad committed intentional assault

496
00:21:57,960 --> 00:21:59,420
and was sentenced to life.

497
00:21:59,720 --> 00:22:00,960
There were seven victims in total.

498
00:22:00,960 --> 00:22:02,000
Two were severely injured,

499
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:03,930
and one was permanently disabled.

500
00:22:04,680 --> 00:22:06,280
My dad also told me to tell you

501
00:22:06,400 --> 00:22:07,600
that it was an ambush.

502
00:22:08,310 --> 00:22:09,240
What do you mean?

503
00:22:09,480 --> 00:22:11,030
First, stab the lower back from behind.

504
00:22:11,030 --> 00:22:12,200
The person turns around,

505
00:22:12,200 --> 00:22:12,860
and then...

506
00:22:19,550 --> 00:22:20,350
Walk forward.

507
00:22:20,360 --> 00:22:21,160
Walk forward.

508
00:22:22,750 --> 00:22:23,280
One stab.

509
00:22:23,550 --> 00:22:24,280
Turn around.

510
00:22:24,480 --> 00:22:25,140
Right here.

511
00:22:25,200 --> 00:22:26,880
One stab, two stabs.

512
00:22:27,160 --> 00:22:27,760
Turn a bit.

513
00:22:29,590 --> 00:22:30,050
Enough.

514
00:22:31,050 --> 00:22:32,710
You're obsessed, aren't you?

515
00:22:36,110 --> 00:22:37,840
The judge won't listen to this.

516
00:22:37,880 --> 00:22:39,010
But right now this is

517
00:22:39,070 --> 00:22:40,960
the closest assumption to the truth.

518
00:22:40,960 --> 00:22:42,160
All this proves is that

519
00:22:42,160 --> 00:22:42,790
Hu Xudong

520
00:22:43,310 --> 00:22:44,440
didn't kill in a fit of passion,

521
00:22:44,440 --> 00:22:45,900
but premeditated murder.

522
00:22:46,020 --> 00:22:47,160
You're just making it worse for him.

523
00:22:47,160 --> 00:22:48,110
What I want to prove is

524
00:22:48,110 --> 00:22:50,030
that Hu Xudong didn't kill anyone.

525
00:22:50,030 --> 00:22:50,440
Get it?

526
00:22:50,880 --> 00:22:51,750
The most important thing now

527
00:22:51,750 --> 00:22:52,400
is reconstructing the scene.

528
00:22:52,400 --> 00:22:54,000
It's like blind men feeling an elephant.

529
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:55,920
We don't have the ability
to solve the case.

530
00:22:55,920 --> 00:22:57,110
Helping the police catch the killer

531
00:22:57,110 --> 00:22:58,130
isn't our job.

532
00:22:58,160 --> 00:22:59,550
We're lawyers.

533
00:22:59,680 --> 00:23:01,000
That's not a lawyer's job!

534
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:02,060
Don't go there yet.

535
00:23:02,830 --> 00:23:03,510
Hu Xudong

536
00:23:04,030 --> 00:23:05,360
has no criminal record,

537
00:23:05,550 --> 00:23:06,040
right?

538
00:23:06,070 --> 00:23:07,400
And he's right-handed.

539
00:23:07,830 --> 00:23:08,640
The killer

540
00:23:08,920 --> 00:23:10,160
is very likely a left-handed person

541
00:23:10,160 --> 00:23:11,480
with a prior assault conviction

542
00:23:11,480 --> 00:23:12,790
who uses a short knife.

543
00:23:13,270 --> 00:23:14,920
Give it a rest
with the left-right hand stuff!

544
00:23:14,920 --> 00:23:16,320
You think you're Sherlock Holmes?

545
00:23:16,320 --> 00:23:16,680
Come on, man.

546
00:23:16,680 --> 00:23:18,770
Filing a lawsuit
isn't like writing a detective novel.

547
00:23:18,770 --> 00:23:20,490
Everything has to be based on evidence.

548
00:23:20,490 --> 00:23:21,520
If we had

549
00:23:21,550 --> 00:23:23,110
a solid alibi,

550
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:24,510
we could fight this case.

551
00:23:24,510 --> 00:23:26,030
But we don't.

552
00:23:26,310 --> 00:23:27,350
Don't keep thinking that way.

553
00:23:27,350 --> 00:23:28,400
Two months ago, we couldn't even

554
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:29,460
see the case files.

555
00:23:29,790 --> 00:23:31,030
What kind of situation is this now?

556
00:23:31,030 --> 00:23:31,640
Now

557
00:23:31,890 --> 00:23:33,680
the amendment
to the Criminal Procedure Law

558
00:23:33,680 --> 00:23:34,770
is an opportunity for Hu Xudong.

559
00:23:34,770 --> 00:23:36,000
We have to seize it for him.

560
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:37,480
I'm not as optimistic as you.

561
00:23:37,480 --> 00:23:39,260
Right now,
our right to review files is limited.

562
00:23:39,260 --> 00:23:40,400
Lin Huaimin has been decent to you,

563
00:23:40,400 --> 00:23:41,160
hasn't obstructed things.

564
00:23:41,160 --> 00:23:42,030
But you still can't

565
00:23:42,030 --> 00:23:43,760
verify the physical evidence.

566
00:23:44,240 --> 00:23:45,400
I'll leave my words here.

567
00:23:45,400 --> 00:23:46,030
There will definitely

568
00:23:46,030 --> 00:23:47,720
be new testimony and evidence

569
00:23:47,750 --> 00:23:48,310
at trial.

570
00:23:48,440 --> 00:23:49,000
What about us?

571
00:23:49,000 --> 00:23:50,720
We've got nothing but

572
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:51,750
logical reasoning

573
00:23:51,750 --> 00:23:53,410
and subjective speculation.

574
00:23:54,110 --> 00:23:55,570
Are you that pessimistic?

575
00:23:55,680 --> 00:23:56,160
Yes.

576
00:23:57,320 --> 00:23:58,240
I'm an optimistic

577
00:23:58,240 --> 00:23:59,070
pessimist.

578
00:23:59,090 --> 00:24:00,330
I always have been.

579
00:24:00,400 --> 00:24:03,060
Otherwise, why wouldn't I
do criminal defense?

580
00:24:07,400 --> 00:24:08,440
So you think

581
00:24:08,770 --> 00:24:10,000
there's no hope for me to plead

582
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:11,060
not guilty for him?

583
00:24:11,680 --> 00:24:12,200
Slim.

584
00:24:13,200 --> 00:24:14,660
Just let the court decide.

585
00:24:14,920 --> 00:24:16,550
If they don't find him guilty,

586
00:24:16,550 --> 00:24:17,480
they won't even hold a trial.

587
00:24:17,480 --> 00:24:19,280
You should be well aware of that.

588
00:24:20,110 --> 00:24:21,030
So according to you,

589
00:24:21,030 --> 00:24:22,560
we should just stop trying.

590
00:24:23,110 --> 00:24:24,110
What's the point?

591
00:24:24,610 --> 00:24:25,880
If everyone thinks like this,

592
00:24:25,880 --> 00:24:27,440
we should just quit.

593
00:24:27,920 --> 00:24:29,250
Why investigate at all?

594
00:24:29,270 --> 00:24:30,720
Just get his old friend Wang Benshan

595
00:24:30,720 --> 00:24:31,520
to defend him.

596
00:24:31,750 --> 00:24:32,930
First-time offender, incidental offender,

597
00:24:32,930 --> 00:24:33,830
with good attitude in pleading guilty,

598
00:24:33,830 --> 00:24:34,790
requesting a lighter sentence.

599
00:24:34,790 --> 00:24:35,390
That's it.

600
00:24:36,030 --> 00:24:36,640
Why bother?

601
00:24:36,640 --> 00:24:38,440
What are we investigating every day for?

602
00:24:38,440 --> 00:24:40,100
Isn't it all for advancement?

603
00:24:43,830 --> 00:24:45,750
I've booked my ticket.
I'm leaving tomorrow.

604
00:24:45,750 --> 00:24:48,150
Ding Rui is about to give birth.
Premature.

605
00:24:54,470 --> 00:24:55,240
Here, take this.

606
00:24:55,240 --> 00:24:56,700
It'll come in handy later.

607
00:24:57,590 --> 00:24:58,080
I don't need it.

608
00:24:58,080 --> 00:24:59,120
Take it!

609
00:25:02,240 --> 00:25:03,300
Put it on the table.

610
00:25:15,530 --> 00:25:18,930
[Binjiang Intermediate People's Court]

611
00:25:18,950 --> 00:25:21,230
[Deputy Court President's Office]

612
00:25:24,720 --> 00:25:25,960
That case in Dashijia Village—

613
00:25:25,960 --> 00:25:27,750
you told the Court Pres.
to put me on it?

614
00:25:27,750 --> 00:25:29,110
The higher-ups take it very seriously.

615
00:25:29,110 --> 00:25:30,510
I also told Court Pres. Qiu

616
00:25:30,510 --> 00:25:32,970
that I want to preside over
the trial myself.

617
00:25:35,210 --> 00:25:35,680
I've been

618
00:25:35,680 --> 00:25:36,570
following the case for a long time.

619
00:25:36,570 --> 00:25:37,970
It's quite interesting.

620
00:25:38,270 --> 00:25:38,920
If it weren't for

621
00:25:38,920 --> 00:25:39,740
Qian Xingliang's matter,

622
00:25:39,740 --> 00:25:41,670
you'd have been promoted long ago.

623
00:25:42,110 --> 00:25:43,240
This is your chance.

624
00:25:46,070 --> 00:25:47,130
There's one thing,

625
00:25:47,510 --> 00:25:49,770
the police came to me after the incident.

626
00:25:50,940 --> 00:25:51,730
Did you give a statement

627
00:25:51,730 --> 00:25:52,440
or sign anything?

628
00:25:52,440 --> 00:25:54,200
No, just an informal chat.

629
00:25:55,330 --> 00:25:56,200
Then it doesn't matter.

630
00:25:56,200 --> 00:25:57,800
You're not a witness either.

631
00:25:59,890 --> 00:26:01,720
Besides, the defendant's defense lawyer

632
00:26:01,720 --> 00:26:02,460
is Chen Yizhong.

633
00:26:02,460 --> 00:26:03,490
Did you know that?

634
00:26:03,960 --> 00:26:05,490
Yeah, I know. What's wrong?

635
00:26:06,240 --> 00:26:08,300
I shouldn't be involved in this case.

636
00:26:09,680 --> 00:26:10,070
Why?

637
00:26:13,200 --> 00:26:14,130
Are you married?

638
00:26:14,720 --> 00:26:15,640
No.

639
00:26:16,200 --> 00:26:17,060
Are you dating?

640
00:26:19,940 --> 00:26:20,880
We were all classmates.

641
00:26:20,880 --> 00:26:22,550
I was classmates with Yizhong too.

642
00:26:22,550 --> 00:26:23,640
There are plenty of lawyers

643
00:26:23,640 --> 00:26:24,750
and prosecutors who were classmates.

644
00:26:24,750 --> 00:26:25,310
So what?

645
00:26:25,510 --> 00:26:26,400
Just because we know each other,

646
00:26:26,400 --> 00:26:28,070
we can't have professional dealings?

647
00:26:28,070 --> 00:26:29,000
You think putting me

648
00:26:29,000 --> 00:26:29,830
on this case

649
00:26:30,110 --> 00:26:30,750
is doing me a favor?

650
00:26:30,750 --> 00:26:31,750
It's not about favors.

651
00:26:31,750 --> 00:26:32,610
It's just work.

652
00:26:37,120 --> 00:26:38,650
I request to recuse myself.

653
00:26:40,030 --> 00:26:41,430
I know you want to take it.

654
00:26:41,790 --> 00:26:42,550
I don't.

655
00:26:43,650 --> 00:26:45,650
I mean, I can't be involved in this.

656
00:26:45,680 --> 00:26:46,810
Do you want to or not?

657
00:26:55,960 --> 00:26:58,550
Who's this gorgeous one
in the mirror?

658
00:26:59,350 --> 00:27:00,350
Did you draw that?

659
00:27:03,550 --> 00:27:04,750
Run.

660
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:10,770
It's Sun and his crew
bringing the chickens.

661
00:27:10,770 --> 00:27:12,090
I... I'll get the door.

662
00:27:12,310 --> 00:27:14,110
I'll draw a little kitty for you.

663
00:27:14,420 --> 00:27:15,270
A little kitty.

664
00:27:15,270 --> 00:27:16,590
Meow, meow.

665
00:27:17,070 --> 00:27:18,530
I'll draw it for you later.

666
00:27:19,200 --> 00:27:20,240
Coming right up.

667
00:27:20,920 --> 00:27:21,380
Coming.

668
00:27:28,070 --> 00:27:28,480
You—

669
00:27:31,550 --> 00:27:32,510
You're here.

670
00:27:36,240 --> 00:27:36,880
Alright.

671
00:27:38,160 --> 00:27:38,960
What's wrong?

672
00:27:39,640 --> 00:27:40,840
You gave up so easily.

673
00:27:41,070 --> 00:27:42,200
I'm innocent.

674
00:27:42,590 --> 00:27:44,390
You'd confess too if you were me.

675
00:27:46,640 --> 00:27:48,480
Why didn't you tell me?

676
00:27:49,350 --> 00:27:50,270
Everything's fine now, isn't it?

677
00:27:50,270 --> 00:27:51,000
No, it's not.

678
00:27:51,030 --> 00:27:52,830
Alright. It's fine.

679
00:27:52,830 --> 00:27:53,360
Alright.

680
00:27:54,960 --> 00:27:55,700
Let go now.

681
00:27:56,550 --> 00:27:57,440
I'm doing fine.

682
00:27:57,790 --> 00:27:58,680
No, you're not.

683
00:28:00,310 --> 00:28:01,030
Next week,

684
00:28:01,320 --> 00:28:02,850
he'll have his second round of chemo.

685
00:28:02,850 --> 00:28:03,710
The doctor said

686
00:28:03,880 --> 00:28:05,680
his condition is stable for now.

687
00:28:06,680 --> 00:28:08,270
It must be hard on you.

688
00:28:09,160 --> 00:28:10,820
Why did you two hide it from me?

689
00:28:12,960 --> 00:28:13,760
Ask him.

690
00:28:14,560 --> 00:28:15,320
First he said

691
00:28:15,350 --> 00:28:17,240
he didn't want to distract you from work.

692
00:28:17,240 --> 00:28:18,480
Then he said

693
00:28:18,590 --> 00:28:19,720
you just got married

694
00:28:19,720 --> 00:28:21,320
and he shouldn't bother you.

695
00:28:22,070 --> 00:28:22,790
He also said

696
00:28:23,240 --> 00:28:24,160
he was afraid you'd worry too much

697
00:28:24,160 --> 00:28:25,510
about Yan Jicai's case.

698
00:28:26,680 --> 00:28:27,140
And now—

699
00:28:27,480 --> 00:28:28,960
he says after this chemo,

700
00:28:29,310 --> 00:28:30,840
he's going back to Bieshan.

701
00:28:31,640 --> 00:28:32,750
Well, I have to go back

702
00:28:32,750 --> 00:28:33,750
and hand things over

703
00:28:33,750 --> 00:28:35,160
properly anyway.

704
00:28:37,110 --> 00:28:37,640
I...

705
00:28:38,350 --> 00:28:39,220
hid it from you.

706
00:28:40,310 --> 00:28:41,130
I was wrong.

707
00:28:41,640 --> 00:28:43,070
I... I apologize.

708
00:28:46,160 --> 00:28:47,550
You always know you're wrong

709
00:28:47,550 --> 00:28:48,410
and apologize.

710
00:28:48,480 --> 00:28:49,440
But in the end?

711
00:28:49,640 --> 00:28:52,240
You do exactly
what you were going to do anyway.

712
00:28:52,440 --> 00:28:52,970
Exactly.

713
00:28:53,550 --> 00:28:55,400
See? That's what
a good education gets you.

714
00:28:55,400 --> 00:28:56,200
You summed him up

715
00:28:56,200 --> 00:28:57,460
in one sentence.

716
00:28:57,880 --> 00:28:59,880
My main worry is that Lihui's

717
00:29:00,410 --> 00:29:01,270
still fixated

718
00:29:01,270 --> 00:29:02,550
on Yan Jicai's case.

719
00:29:05,490 --> 00:29:06,890
If she finds out I'm sick,

720
00:29:07,350 --> 00:29:09,810
s-she'd definitely
not be able to sit still.

721
00:29:10,960 --> 00:29:12,680
We sent an official letter

722
00:29:13,000 --> 00:29:14,550
to the Nanlu Procuratorate.

723
00:29:14,550 --> 00:29:15,480
No response yet.

724
00:29:16,110 --> 00:29:18,310
Looks like there's a lot of resistance.

725
00:29:19,920 --> 00:29:21,160
There sure is.

726
00:29:22,880 --> 00:29:24,790
Now that I'm at the Nanlu Procuratorate,

727
00:29:24,790 --> 00:29:26,990
and with my relationship with Jianmin,

728
00:29:27,310 --> 00:29:28,910
I feel like my hands are tied.

729
00:29:28,960 --> 00:29:30,830
I'm going to put it aside for now.

730
00:29:32,270 --> 00:29:33,070
That's right.

731
00:29:33,790 --> 00:29:34,770
You should put it aside.

732
00:29:34,770 --> 00:29:36,330
Look, you're still young.

733
00:29:36,590 --> 00:29:38,110
You can't sacrifice your

734
00:29:38,370 --> 00:29:40,090
career and life for it,

735
00:29:40,240 --> 00:29:40,680
right?

736
00:29:42,440 --> 00:29:43,970
You shouldn't feel guilty.

737
00:29:44,750 --> 00:29:45,400
Besides,

738
00:29:45,640 --> 00:29:46,830
you've got me.

739
00:29:47,750 --> 00:29:49,000
You're sick.

740
00:29:50,030 --> 00:29:52,160
I'm in good health.

741
00:29:52,440 --> 00:29:53,480
I'm fine.

742
00:29:53,500 --> 00:29:55,670
I walk 10,000 steps a day.

743
00:29:56,030 --> 00:29:56,920
Alright.

744
00:29:58,400 --> 00:29:59,310
Alright.

745
00:29:59,310 --> 00:30:00,480
Alright. This is enough.

746
00:30:00,480 --> 00:30:00,810
What?

747
00:30:02,720 --> 00:30:03,780
It's getting late.

748
00:30:04,030 --> 00:30:05,430
You should get some rest.

749
00:30:05,590 --> 00:30:07,510
I'll take Lihui to the guesthouse.

750
00:30:07,510 --> 00:30:08,440
We'll come back tomorrow.

751
00:30:08,440 --> 00:30:08,720
You—

752
00:30:08,880 --> 00:30:09,330
Prosecutor You,

753
00:30:09,330 --> 00:30:10,130
I want to stay with my mentor

754
00:30:10,130 --> 00:30:10,920
for a while longer.

755
00:30:10,920 --> 00:30:12,650
Your luggage is still in my car.

756
00:30:12,720 --> 00:30:13,270
Let's go.

757
00:30:16,510 --> 00:30:17,200
Go now.

758
00:30:26,440 --> 00:30:27,370
Prosecutor You.

759
00:30:28,310 --> 00:30:29,440
Is something wrong?

760
00:30:30,720 --> 00:30:32,450
A message came from the prison.

761
00:30:32,750 --> 00:30:34,410
Yan Jicai committed suicide.

762
00:30:36,620 --> 00:30:37,390
Let's go.

763
00:31:00,880 --> 00:31:01,910
Here, have some water.

764
00:31:01,910 --> 00:31:02,680
Thank you.

765
00:31:07,830 --> 00:31:08,790
When did you first

766
00:31:08,790 --> 00:31:09,820
meet Hu Xudong?

767
00:31:10,510 --> 00:31:11,640
We grew up together.

768
00:31:13,310 --> 00:31:14,960
Has his temper

769
00:31:15,230 --> 00:31:16,490
always been like this?

770
00:31:17,750 --> 00:31:19,810
He definitely has a terrible temper.

771
00:31:19,960 --> 00:31:21,920
But if you say he killed someone,

772
00:31:23,160 --> 00:31:24,220
I don't believe it.

773
00:31:24,790 --> 00:31:26,310
He's all bark, no bite.

774
00:31:26,720 --> 00:31:28,110
No real guts.

775
00:31:28,880 --> 00:31:31,680
But he has a kind heart.

776
00:31:32,270 --> 00:31:33,600
What makes you say that?

777
00:31:33,920 --> 00:31:36,250
He lived next door
to that Yin Ping, right?

778
00:31:36,960 --> 00:31:39,510
He's been helping
his grandmother with chores

779
00:31:39,510 --> 00:31:40,480
for years.

780
00:31:41,500 --> 00:31:42,900
And what did he get for it?

781
00:31:43,030 --> 00:31:44,360
Got blamed by everyone.

782
00:31:45,030 --> 00:31:45,960
Tell me about it.

783
00:31:49,790 --> 00:31:51,720
Yin Ping had an uncle.

784
00:31:51,720 --> 00:31:52,120
Right?

785
00:31:52,590 --> 00:31:54,450
Don't even mention that bastard.

786
00:31:55,310 --> 00:31:56,770
When his mother was alive,

787
00:31:56,830 --> 00:31:58,140
he was nowhere to be found.

788
00:31:58,140 --> 00:32:00,040
Now that she's dead,

789
00:32:00,510 --> 00:32:01,680
he comes back for compensation.

790
00:32:01,680 --> 00:32:02,790
Is he even human?

791
00:32:05,660 --> 00:32:07,750
That day you drank with Hu Xudong,

792
00:32:07,750 --> 00:32:09,240
how late did you drink until?

793
00:32:09,240 --> 00:32:11,570
The cops have asked me that several times.

794
00:32:11,880 --> 00:32:13,280
I really can't remember.

795
00:32:13,440 --> 00:32:14,510
I drank too much.

796
00:32:16,480 --> 00:32:17,350
After you two

797
00:32:17,590 --> 00:32:19,590
finished drinking, was the light on

798
00:32:19,640 --> 00:32:20,370
when he left?

799
00:32:20,880 --> 00:32:21,720
Light?

800
00:32:23,590 --> 00:32:24,390
Yeah, I think.

801
00:32:25,110 --> 00:32:25,660
Off you go.

802
00:32:25,660 --> 00:32:27,260
You should get some rest too.

803
00:32:28,030 --> 00:32:28,830
Clean this up.

804
00:32:30,400 --> 00:32:30,750
Go.

805
00:32:31,270 --> 00:32:32,720
Happy wedding, buddy.

806
00:32:33,720 --> 00:32:35,720
Anyway, I fell asleep after he left.

807
00:32:36,000 --> 00:32:37,680
I got up to pee
in the middle of the night.

808
00:32:37,680 --> 00:32:39,200
I don't know what happened to the light.

809
00:32:39,200 --> 00:32:40,520
It just wouldn't turn on.

810
00:32:40,520 --> 00:32:42,070
How long did you sleep in between?

811
00:32:42,070 --> 00:32:43,110
Do you have any idea?

812
00:32:43,110 --> 00:32:44,370
I really can't recall.

813
00:32:53,230 --> 00:32:54,300
Around 3 a.m.,

814
00:32:54,680 --> 00:32:56,440
while everyone else was asleep,

815
00:32:56,440 --> 00:32:56,880
he tied his pant leg

816
00:32:56,880 --> 00:32:58,140
to the upper bunk rail.

817
00:32:58,750 --> 00:32:59,550
Fortunately,

818
00:32:59,720 --> 00:33:01,320
his cellmates were vigilant

819
00:33:01,350 --> 00:33:02,270
and saved him.

820
00:33:02,550 --> 00:33:03,810
Then he bit his tongue.

821
00:33:04,240 --> 00:33:06,240
So many people would be implicated.

822
00:33:13,680 --> 00:33:14,280
Yan Jicai,

823
00:33:14,920 --> 00:33:15,550
do you think

824
00:33:15,550 --> 00:33:16,880
since I was transferred

825
00:33:16,920 --> 00:33:18,110
and Prosecutor Guo is away,

826
00:33:18,110 --> 00:33:19,550
no one will care about your case?

827
00:33:19,550 --> 00:33:20,150
Is that it?

828
00:33:32,700 --> 00:33:35,170
[Cancer]

829
00:33:40,440 --> 00:33:42,100
We've been keeping it secret.

830
00:33:42,680 --> 00:33:43,830
Who told him?

831
00:33:46,030 --> 00:33:46,440
Yes.

832
00:33:47,350 --> 00:33:48,240
Prosecutor Guo isn't

833
00:33:48,240 --> 00:33:49,440
doing well right now,

834
00:33:49,510 --> 00:33:51,350
but he's actively
cooperating with treatment.

835
00:33:51,350 --> 00:33:53,280
I came back specifically for this.

836
00:33:54,240 --> 00:33:56,240
By the way, I'll show you something.

837
00:33:56,310 --> 00:33:57,440
I took it a month ago.

838
00:33:58,420 --> 00:33:59,070
Lie down.

839
00:33:59,550 --> 00:34:00,150
Yan Jicai,

840
00:34:00,440 --> 00:34:02,440
even if we can't overturn your conviction,

841
00:34:02,440 --> 00:34:03,510
as long as you behave

842
00:34:03,510 --> 00:34:04,720
and work toward a sentence commutation,

843
00:34:04,720 --> 00:34:05,980
by the time you get out,

844
00:34:06,270 --> 00:34:08,670
you can still see her
graduate from college.

845
00:34:08,670 --> 00:34:10,400
Think about what you should do.

846
00:34:11,000 --> 00:34:11,600
I have more

847
00:34:11,610 --> 00:34:13,010
worthwhile things to do.

848
00:34:14,190 --> 00:34:16,120
This is my last time reminding you.

849
00:34:17,480 --> 00:34:18,280
It's up to you.

850
00:34:21,550 --> 00:34:22,080
Lie down.

851
00:34:24,030 --> 00:34:25,159
Lie down. Lie still.

852
00:34:25,920 --> 00:34:27,489
I'll leave the photo with you.

853
00:34:27,489 --> 00:34:28,440
Whether to give it to him and when,

854
00:34:28,440 --> 00:34:29,159
you decide.

855
00:34:32,550 --> 00:34:33,610
How's your mentor?

856
00:34:35,150 --> 00:34:36,010
I believe

857
00:34:36,630 --> 00:34:38,280
God won't be so heartless.

858
00:34:46,300 --> 00:34:47,360
Got everything. Let's go.

859
00:34:47,360 --> 00:34:47,770
Sir.

860
00:34:48,190 --> 00:34:48,590
Sir.

861
00:34:50,550 --> 00:34:51,000
Sir.

862
00:34:51,590 --> 00:34:52,150
Well,

863
00:34:53,070 --> 00:34:53,550
lately,

864
00:34:54,070 --> 00:34:55,199
anything new found?

865
00:34:56,320 --> 00:34:56,760
Yeah.

866
00:34:57,230 --> 00:34:57,830
What is it?

867
00:34:58,760 --> 00:34:59,590
The cigarettes your buddy

868
00:34:59,590 --> 00:35:01,120
gave me last time were fake.

869
00:35:11,210 --> 00:35:13,960
[Lawyer Chen, the court
wants me to hear this case.]

870
00:35:21,290 --> 00:35:22,230
Yu Gaoyuan asked you

871
00:35:22,230 --> 00:35:23,360
to join the case?

872
00:35:27,880 --> 00:35:29,680
I've known him for so many years,

873
00:35:30,480 --> 00:35:32,340
but I still don't understand him.

874
00:35:32,590 --> 00:35:33,800
You're not the only one.

875
00:35:33,800 --> 00:35:35,000
Who understands him?

876
00:35:36,720 --> 00:35:38,970
I used to think he was just

877
00:35:39,000 --> 00:35:39,990
a bit insecure,

878
00:35:40,480 --> 00:35:41,360
a bit proud,

879
00:35:42,150 --> 00:35:43,400
a bit power-hungry,

880
00:35:43,840 --> 00:35:44,880
and a bit jealous.

881
00:35:46,480 --> 00:35:48,940
Now he's getting
more and more complicated.

882
00:35:50,320 --> 00:35:51,110
But it's easy for him

883
00:35:51,110 --> 00:35:52,110
to see through me.

884
00:35:53,840 --> 00:35:54,510
He's right.

885
00:35:56,510 --> 00:35:57,150
Honestly,

886
00:35:58,800 --> 00:35:59,840
I really do

887
00:35:59,840 --> 00:36:01,100
want to take this case,

888
00:36:03,400 --> 00:36:04,110
even though I know

889
00:36:04,110 --> 00:36:05,510
there's not much I can do.

890
00:36:08,160 --> 00:36:09,630
Who would have thought that

891
00:36:09,630 --> 00:36:10,890
the few of us from Nanyu

892
00:36:11,110 --> 00:36:12,440
would almost all gather

893
00:36:12,870 --> 00:36:13,800
on this one case?

894
00:36:13,880 --> 00:36:14,920
Exactly.

895
00:36:15,610 --> 00:36:16,940
Just missing Lihui now.

896
00:36:18,070 --> 00:36:19,330
So we have to work hard.

897
00:36:19,880 --> 00:36:21,610
Let's not let Lihui down again.

898
00:36:26,440 --> 00:36:27,900
Sorry to keep you waiting.

899
00:36:28,000 --> 00:36:29,530
What happened to your face?

900
00:36:30,510 --> 00:36:33,110
I... I just handled a

901
00:36:33,110 --> 00:36:34,110
difficult case,

902
00:36:34,670 --> 00:36:35,470
and solved it.

903
00:36:37,320 --> 00:36:38,030
Have a seat.

904
00:36:38,320 --> 00:36:38,710
Okay.

905
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:40,710
Mr. Qin,

906
00:36:41,440 --> 00:36:41,960
you

907
00:36:42,150 --> 00:36:43,750
always go all out every time.

908
00:36:44,000 --> 00:36:44,670
It makes me

909
00:36:44,960 --> 00:36:46,590
both worried and happy.

910
00:36:50,230 --> 00:36:51,710
I understand why you're worried.

911
00:36:51,710 --> 00:36:52,910
But why are you happy?

912
00:36:53,880 --> 00:36:55,510
I'm happy because

913
00:36:55,960 --> 00:36:57,360
I found the right person.

914
00:37:00,280 --> 00:37:00,670
I...

915
00:37:01,050 --> 00:37:02,710
I'm already married.

916
00:37:02,740 --> 00:37:04,340
My kid is pretty grown up now.

917
00:37:05,190 --> 00:37:05,590
You...

918
00:37:06,800 --> 00:37:08,480
You're really good at joking.

919
00:37:09,230 --> 00:37:10,890
I'm not looking for a husband.

920
00:37:11,000 --> 00:37:12,580
I'm looking for a partner.

921
00:37:15,230 --> 00:37:16,030
Our company's

922
00:37:16,070 --> 00:37:16,920
business in Nanlu

923
00:37:16,920 --> 00:37:18,550
is getting bigger and bigger.

924
00:37:18,550 --> 00:37:20,280
We need to hire a legal advisor.

925
00:37:20,320 --> 00:37:21,670
We applied to the boss,

926
00:37:21,880 --> 00:37:22,940
and he approved it.

927
00:37:23,030 --> 00:37:23,440
You

928
00:37:23,760 --> 00:37:25,620
are the most suitable candidate.

929
00:37:25,630 --> 00:37:26,490
Legal advisor?

930
00:37:28,700 --> 00:37:29,790
May I know

931
00:37:29,810 --> 00:37:31,630
how much your annual salary is here,

932
00:37:31,630 --> 00:37:32,360
roughly?

933
00:37:36,550 --> 00:37:38,810
You don't have to say
if you don't want to.

934
00:37:39,590 --> 00:37:40,150
Well,

935
00:37:41,110 --> 00:37:42,920
I'm a partner in the firm.

936
00:37:43,440 --> 00:37:45,360
I have a base salary,

937
00:37:46,160 --> 00:37:48,290
commissions, year-end bonus,

938
00:37:48,320 --> 00:37:49,000
and dividends—

939
00:37:49,000 --> 00:37:49,660
Alright.

940
00:37:51,320 --> 00:37:52,650
How about this, Mr. Qin?

941
00:37:53,030 --> 00:37:54,030
Our company can offer you

942
00:37:54,030 --> 00:37:55,160
15,000 yuan a month,

943
00:37:56,130 --> 00:37:57,800
plus a double-year-end bonus.

944
00:37:57,800 --> 00:37:58,670
All in all,

945
00:37:58,960 --> 00:38:00,690
it's about over 200,000 a year.

946
00:38:01,070 --> 00:38:02,070
What do you think?

947
00:38:04,440 --> 00:38:05,000
But

948
00:38:05,510 --> 00:38:06,880
you have to work in Nanlu.

949
00:38:06,880 --> 00:38:08,080
Our company is there.

950
00:38:08,150 --> 00:38:08,640
Also,

951
00:38:08,960 --> 00:38:10,690
you have to rent your own place.

952
00:38:21,520 --> 00:38:22,320
About this,

953
00:38:23,440 --> 00:38:25,150
I have to discuss it

954
00:38:25,280 --> 00:38:26,210
with my partner.

955
00:38:26,440 --> 00:38:26,800
Sure.

956
00:38:27,230 --> 00:38:28,030
Think about it

957
00:38:28,360 --> 00:38:29,960
and get back to me as soon as possible.

958
00:38:29,960 --> 00:38:30,880
Okay.

959
00:38:33,800 --> 00:38:34,460
Wait for me.

960
00:38:34,760 --> 00:38:35,800
Let me go get changed,

961
00:38:35,800 --> 00:38:37,030
and we'll go have dinner together.

962
00:38:37,030 --> 00:38:37,400
Okay.

963
00:38:37,400 --> 00:38:38,310
Come on, drink more of it.

964
00:38:38,310 --> 00:38:39,110
-Okay.
-Here.

965
00:38:39,190 --> 00:38:39,520
Okay.

966
00:38:40,550 --> 00:38:41,010
Cheers.

967
00:39:04,550 --> 00:39:06,030
Where did you go drinking?

968
00:39:06,320 --> 00:39:07,170
And with whom?

969
00:39:11,070 --> 00:39:13,070
Which tramp were you with this time?

970
00:39:20,380 --> 00:39:21,760
I stewed black chicken and cooked dishes

971
00:39:21,760 --> 00:39:23,090
at home waiting for you,

972
00:39:23,150 --> 00:39:25,750
and you went out
living it up with someone else!

973
00:39:27,550 --> 00:39:28,950
What are you trying to do?

974
00:39:32,920 --> 00:39:34,110
Svoboda.

975
00:39:35,880 --> 00:39:37,050
Svoboda.

976
00:39:37,360 --> 00:39:38,490
What does that mean?

977
00:39:40,720 --> 00:39:41,920
Svoboda.

978
00:39:44,480 --> 00:39:45,410
What do you mean?

979
00:39:46,840 --> 00:39:48,230
Svoboda.

980
00:40:04,800 --> 00:40:06,860
Tell me, what have I ever asked of you?

981
00:40:08,030 --> 00:40:09,190
Just that you'd

982
00:40:09,190 --> 00:40:10,760
live a good life with me.

983
00:40:11,960 --> 00:40:13,760
Have I ever been disloyal to you?

984
00:40:14,920 --> 00:40:16,180
I may have a bad temper,

985
00:40:16,860 --> 00:40:18,110
but I've always taken care of you

986
00:40:18,110 --> 00:40:19,060
and this family.

987
00:40:19,800 --> 00:40:21,460
Tell me, what else do you want?

988
00:40:22,190 --> 00:40:23,710
What else do you want?

989
00:40:25,630 --> 00:40:27,070
Svoboda.

990
00:41:04,890 --> 00:41:08,190
[Gui Xiaotang, General Manager
of Guangdong Dingji Trading Group]

991
00:41:18,150 --> 00:41:19,400
It's not that I don't support you.

992
00:41:19,400 --> 00:41:21,460
I'm just advising you to be cautious.

993
00:41:21,840 --> 00:41:22,920
If you want to get things done,

994
00:41:22,920 --> 00:41:24,580
you better keep a low profile.

995
00:41:25,400 --> 00:41:27,720
If you can't get it done
with a low profile,

996
00:41:27,720 --> 00:41:29,720
a high profile
will only make things worse.

997
00:41:29,720 --> 00:41:30,670
But I can't think of

998
00:41:30,670 --> 00:41:31,590
any other way.

999
00:41:31,840 --> 00:41:33,760
Let's not think about
anything else for now.

1000
00:41:33,760 --> 00:41:35,030
Provincial media, city media—

1001
00:41:35,030 --> 00:41:37,030
which outlet would dare publish it?

1002
00:41:40,590 --> 00:41:42,120
What about going higher up?

1003
00:41:44,920 --> 00:41:47,250
Have you thought about the consequences?

1004
00:41:52,070 --> 00:41:53,670
Prosecutor You gave this to me.

1005
00:41:53,670 --> 00:41:54,760
My mentor's medal.

1006
00:41:56,810 --> 00:41:58,540
I want him to wear it on his chest

1007
00:41:58,760 --> 00:41:59,760
while he's alive,

1008
00:42:01,450 --> 00:42:02,670
not have it pressed under the Party flag

1009
00:42:02,670 --> 00:42:03,600
after he's gone.

1010
00:42:05,630 --> 00:42:07,760
I don't want him to leave with regrets.

1011
00:42:16,510 --> 00:42:18,040
If it really gets reported,

1012
00:42:19,480 --> 00:42:21,410
there will be many possibilities.

1013
00:42:21,510 --> 00:42:23,110
It could turn out very badly,

1014
00:42:23,550 --> 00:42:25,280
or nothing might happen at all.

1015
00:42:26,070 --> 00:42:28,230
The wrongful conviction
could be overturned,

1016
00:42:28,230 --> 00:42:30,150
or the original verdict could stand.

1017
00:42:30,150 --> 00:42:30,950
Worst case...

1018
00:42:31,360 --> 00:42:33,690
Worst case, the original verdict stands,

1019
00:42:34,030 --> 00:42:34,880
and I resign.

1020
00:42:42,190 --> 00:42:42,760
Lihui,

1021
00:42:43,800 --> 00:42:45,550
we've really done our best.

1022
00:42:47,290 --> 00:42:47,840
To be honest,

1023
00:42:47,840 --> 00:42:49,000
going all out like this

1024
00:42:49,000 --> 00:42:50,290
for Yan Jicai—

1025
00:42:50,880 --> 00:42:52,480
the cost is too high.

1026
00:42:53,150 --> 00:42:55,070
I'm not just doing this for Yan Jicai.

1027
00:42:55,070 --> 00:42:57,070
It's also for justice under the law,

1028
00:42:57,840 --> 00:42:58,760
for my mentor,

1029
00:43:00,710 --> 00:43:02,110
and for Yan Jicai's wife

1030
00:43:02,110 --> 00:43:02,810
and daughter.
